 "_notes": [
  "CastManifest (src/assets/art/manifest.ts) plus these notes. Every sprite is stored at 2x the yard's CSS size on the set's camera: 176 px per metre of the orthographic view (a metre straight up is 152.4 px; set.json's map.ppm, 139.14, is a metre along a lawn edge in the same camera), so the yard draws each at 0.5 and never rescales one breed differently.",
  "scale: corgiLength is the corgi's moving pose, trimmed width, in px at 2x; each other breed's moving pose is a fixed ratio of it (beagle 1.15, collie 1.35, poodle 1.3, Lab 1.55, golden 1.6), and its sit and sleep share that scale; the crew (crew-*) is crewToStandingGolden x the golden's standing height, and the second crew member (crew2-*: a different adult in the same uniform, so two or three staff on the floor are not one person repeated) is 1.07 x the first one's height.",
  "anchor: the ground point in the image's pixels (a dog: between its near and far feet; the crew: between the shoes). facing: every sprite faces right, along the camera-facing diagonal toward the lower right; mirror for the other diagonal (gate 5). No shadow is drawn in any sprite (gate 3).",
  "coat: the generated coat of each breed (golden gold, Lab black, poodle brown, corgi red, collie black, beagle tricolour) and its recolours in code (gate 6); the yellow Lab is its own generated strip, at the Lab's ratio; docs/art-provenance/cast/README.md has every step."
 ]
}
